<p><strong><font color="blue">FAYDEDAR THREAD THING</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, May 29, 2001 by <a href="mailto:santerre@vallisscortor.com">Santerre</a></small><br>Figured I'd post this here as I will be sending people to read this tongiht if they ask what we are doing!!!<br><br>----Guys even though I am having a super-busy day at the office here and have something I need to fix before I leave but still want to do this tonight. We can set up at 7cst-8est-1gmt at the docks in Oasis of Marr. The dragon is in Timourous Deep in the "oasis" island. This is in the south central part of the zone. It looks like a huge circular wall in the water. Underwater at about -12000, -3000 there is an underwater cave through the wall. THere is a smaller circle wall inside that also has an underwater cave into it. Inside is a lagoon area with some shops. There should be a dwarf on the beach - he is the trigger.<br>We need 3-4 groups, including Nitrain, Larla, and Artallen (for good buffs) in order to try. Tanks need to be 50+, caster we can get away with 47th or so, lower on /assist healers/bards.<br><br>When we have enough with will form groups of 5. everyone will completely debuff. Each group will be responsibile for getting and keeping up 4 "junk" buffs. Acceptable junk buffs are: Levitate/DMF, Resist Cold/Poison/Disease, SoW, etc. Do NOT use see invis. Longer duration the better. The idea here is for Fayd to dispel as few buffs as possible. After the 4 buffs you may self-buff leaving enough slots as below. <br><br>Buffs will come in order by adding Larla, Nitrain, Artallen, and myself to the group:<br>Larla: Focus, Acumen, STA.<br>Nitrain: Aeologism.<br>Artallen: Clarity and/or Haste, GRM<br>Santerre: Circle of Winter.<br><br>If we have a mage, we will circle him for boon of immolation as well (BIG help w/ FR).<br><br>You should have your FR gear on. 100FR unbuffed will definately help us here. This means you sacrifice you primary casting stat or melee stats for FR. I honestly dont remember Fayd fearing people... but I take Crydees word for it better safe than sorry. MR would be good as well. Emerald and... um... hematite rings will add FR, even at cost of like 100pp.<br><br>Fight will go as follows: Once groups are established we will start a 30 minute timer to buff. Group leaders make sure you know who is ready, in what order, and who has what junk buffs. At the end of the period, all tanks and Larla line up on the beach, and all casters/pets in the tunnel... all must stand.<br><br>Let me repeat that: ALL MUST STAND!!!!!<br><br>Our primary tank (Gert or Bobbib or worst case Sorack /shudder) will SIT on the beach. I will turn in item and run to cave. Fayd will spawn shortly thereafter and go right for the sitting primary tank. That tank needs to aggro for 10-15 seconds before other tanks jump in and larla begins to slow. Faydedar should always be facing AWAY FROM THE CASTERS!!!!. If he ping-pongs we will all die.<br><br>Clerics should be healing ONLY THOSE WITH AGGRO (Sorack Bobbib Gert Nevtay). Those that are taking damage too fast from fire will not be healed by a cleric... get your resist gear! Backup healers can healer group members fire damage or even better /assist heal.<br><br>At 75% pets go in. At 50% casters open fire. Cold works nicely on Fayd, magic will land as well. Don't even try fire, don't try RFS. <br><br>Thats all I can say for now PLEASE read this and PLEASE come! Seeya there!<br><br>----<br><br>Thanks, Santerre.</p>
