<p><strong><font color="blue">Heads up, patch on the way for May 30th.</font> </strong><small>Posted Tuesday, May 15, 2001 by <a href="mailto:silvermaine@vallisscortor.com">Silvermaine</a></small><br>Important News Regarding Upcoming Patch  <br> <br>Our next patch is planned for May 30th, probably some time in the wee morning hours here on the West Coast. <br><br>The important part of the message is not that, though. It's this:<br><br>Due to some of the things we are going to be doing, there is a small chance that some corpses might disappear during the patch. GMs will have the ability to verify any corpses that are lost. That means that they can help you get them back if you do indeed lose one. It also means that I should remind everyone that attempting to scam a GM about a lost corpse could mean banning. <br><br>So please make certain that you have as many of your corpses cleaned up as possible before the next patch. We're not expecting a lot of corpses to disappear, but the fewer lying around, the less chance of them disappearing.  <br></p>
